A||N||5||gmata||HELP!!! Car won't start at times...||||11||
Z||000000||gmata||11-06-2001||11:03 AM||||It seems that might car won't start at times.  We found a bad rotor and replaced it last week.  We thought we had fixed the problem, but it is back.  I have been driving the car for the last week and it was starting fine.  When I came to work on Monday, it didn't want to start.  I towed the car to the shop.  When it arrived, they were able to start the car without doing anything to it.  Any ideas why the car starts at times and not others?<P>-Gus<BR>||||reg||11
Z||000001||Old Lar||11-06-2001||11:23 AM||||Check for loose battery terminal. I have had similiar problem on two Fieros.  I disconnected terminal, made sure they were clean, reconnected, the problem went away.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Old Lar (edited 11-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||gmata||11-06-2001||11:30 AM||||I don't know if it is a battery connection problem.  When I turn the ignition, the car wants to start, but doesn't turn over.  Correct me if I'm wrong, but if it was a battery connection problem wouldn't it make a clicking noise?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||11-06-2001||05:07 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by gmata:<BR><B>I don't know if it is a battery connection problem.  When I turn the ignition, the car wants to start, but doesn't turn over.  Correct me if I'm wrong, but if it was a battery connection problem wouldn't it make a clicking noise?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>What do you mean, the car wants to start but doesn't turn over?<P>Clicking is a sign of a weak battery.<P>Just check the terminal connection.  Do the easist things first.  Then check the connection to the starter, starter ground etc.  There may be a dead spot in the starter.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||gmata||11-06-2001||05:37 PM||||When starting the engine, I don't hear a clicking noise.  The engine is trying to start, but has no spark or fire...  I replace the ignition coil, distributor, wires, spark plugs, and the wire going from the coil to the distributor about five months ago.  Don't know what might be causing it to not fire at times.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Gary W||11-06-2001||09:37 PM||||Did you check for fuel? What engine?<P>(Oops, rotor, must be the V6)<BR>If it cranks and won't start, check for fuel at the schraeder valve on the injector rail. If you have a spark tester, check at least one plug from each side of the engine.<p>[This message has been edited by Gary W (edited 11-06-2001).]||||reg||1
